  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Natural disasters such as floods, hurricanes and earthquakes can cause rivers to reverse. Letterpress type is inversely carved so that words read properly when inked and pressed onto paper. Tintypes capture mirror images of their subjects. Just like multiplying two negatives results in a positive, making a wet plate of letterpress characters produced the cover's right reading inset tintype"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"...The interior images are inkjet printed, while this Garamond text is LaserJet printed on 50 lb., double-sided, matte, Red River Paper from Dallas, TX. The bookcloth is Canapetta. The cotton rag covers and endsheets were handmade at the University of Georgia's study abroad facility in Cortona, Italy. The fan was printed using a polymer plate produced by Boxcar Press in Syracuse, NY"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Jay Gould furnished the Rubens letterpress type used for the book's title. Dave Hyams provided tireless guidance during the making of these tintypes. Jim Sherraden at Hatch Show Print advised in regards to wording and inks. Nicole Duet assisted in the selection and sequencing of the book's images"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hardbound photo book. Tintype embedded in the cover. Colophon states, "Tintypes capture mirror images of their subjects. Just like multiplying two negatives results in a positive, making a wet plate of letterpress characters produced the cover's right reading inset tintype." Deluxe gatefold edition. </subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited edition of 25 copies. SCAD Atlanta owns 9/25.</subfield>
  </datafield>
